<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria to auction three floater T-bill issues.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria to auction three floater T-bill issues.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer three floating interest T-bill issues with maturities of six, nine and 12 months and a total par value of 20 billion levs at auctions on Monday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The issues will be offered with no minimum acceptable prices set in advance.</p>
<p>Interest on the issues is due at maturity. It equals the central bank main interest rate for each of the issues and is adjusted every time the rate is changed by the central bank.</p>
<p>The main interest rate is now set at 48.72 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the offers follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	   BG3037897025	 BG3037997023</p>
<p> Maturity		 six months	   nine months</p>
<p> Par value		10.0 bln levs	5.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	   June 9		 June 9</p>
<p> Issue date	     June 11		June 11</p>
<p> Maturity date	  December 10	  March 11, 1998</p>
<p> Issue number	   BG3038097021</p>
<p> Maturity		 12 months</p>
<p> Par value		5.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	   June 9</p>
<p> Issue date	     June 11</p>
<p> Maturity date	  June 10, 1998</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
